# Bug in Community MySQL : after transformation to derived table and merging, table t3 is in the table list of select#5 but has a select_lex pointer == select#2. This in turn poses problems during Item cloning, so we catch this situation early and go to non-PQ execution for select#5 (but not the others). Test query inspired by one in subquery_scalar_to_derived.test.
CREATE TABLE t1(a INT);
CREATE TABLE t2(a INT);
CREATE TABLE t3(c INT);
set @save_opt_s = @@optimizer_switch;
set optimizer_switch="subquery_to_derived=on";
